    "narrative": "The highlight of today\u2019s slate for LawDog is **Lawrence Butler**, who commands our highest efficiency rating at 73.47. Facing Zack Littell, **Butler** benefits from a massive 13% boost from his platoon advantage and a favorable park factor, making him an essential anchor in the outfield. Following closely in the \"Strong\" tier are **Dylan Beavers** (61.84) and **Yainer Diaz** (61.74). **Diaz** is particularly well-positioned against Triston Rogers, whose 4.71 xERA provides a clear runway for production. We are also looking for significant output from **JJ Bleday**, whose 61.32 score is bolstered by an elite 14% park factor, even against a tough arm in Sugano. While **Bryce Harper** (59.49) sits just shy of the 60+ threshold, his elite xwOBA of 0.391 ensures he remains a must-start in the utility spot despite facing a veteran like Sean Manaea.\n\nOur toughest roster exclusion today was **Jung Hoo Lee** (46.06). While **Lee**\u2019s platoon edge against Woo provides some value, he ultimately fell short of our high-performing starters who possess superior situational alignment, particularly **Masyn Winn**, who provides critical stolen base upside\u2014a priority given our league's scarcity constraints. We also opted to bench **Ryan Waldschmidt** (45.19), as his lower spot in the order suppresses his efficiency relative to the rest of the lineup. As a reminder, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains sidelined on the IL, leaving us to rely on our active core to maintain our Roto standing. Monitor the final lineups closely; **Lawrence Butler** is currently penciled in based on a projected #6 spot, and any shift lower in the order could marginally impact his output, though his matchup remains favorable regardless.",
